-- חוק הביטוח הלאומי [נוסח משולב], התשנ"ה-1995 — section 22: how the
-- Institute's own employees are appointed and on what terms they serve, which
-- the 3.3.1999 pension agreement cites; and section 50(א): for how many
-- weeks an insured woman is paid maternity pay. The text is
-- laws/national-insurance-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים
-- הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy. Which periods count as insured (50(ב)–(ז))
-- is not encoded: the months insured are inputs.

IMPORT prelude

§ `חוק הביטוח הלאומי — עובדי המוסד ותקופת דמי הלידה`

§§ `22`

-- (א): within the establishment the Minister approved, the Institute's
-- management appoints the rest of its employees and sets their duties and
-- powers — save its actuary (appointed under §24) and its branch managers
-- (under §23). (ב): their appointment follows the rules for appointing
-- State employees, with the changes the matter requires, and their terms of
-- work are a State employee's.
@ref law:22
DECLARE `employee of the Institute, under section 22` IS ONE OF
    `the Institute's actuary, appointed under section 24`
    `a branch manager, appointed under section 23`
    `another employee of the Institute`

@ref law:22
GIVEN e IS AN `employee of the Institute, under section 22`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the management appoints him under section 22(א)` e IF
    e EQUALS `another employee of the Institute`

-- (ב): so the rules a State employee is appointed by — a special contract
-- among them — reach the Institute's employees, and their terms are the
-- State's.
@ref law:22
`the rules for appointing State employees reach the Institute's employees under section 22(ב)` MEANS TRUE

@ref law:22
`the Institute's employees serve on a State employee's terms under section 22(ב)` MEANS TRUE

§§ `50`

-- (א)(1): 15 weeks, if insurance contributions were paid for 10 of the 14
-- months before the determining day or for 15 of the 22 months before it;
-- (2): 8 weeks, if for 6 of the 14. Otherwise none under this section.
@ref law:50
GIVEN `months insured of the 14 before the determining day` IS A NUMBER
      `months insured of the 22 before the determining day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of maternity pay` `months insured of the 14 before the determining day` `months insured of the 22 before the determining day` IS
    IF `months insured of the 14 before the determining day` AT LEAST 10
       OR `months insured of the 22 before the determining day` AT LEAST 15
    THEN 15
    ELSE IF `months insured of the 14 before the determining day` AT LEAST 6
         THEN 8
         ELSE 0

#ASSERT `weeks of maternity pay` 14 22 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `weeks of maternity pay` 9 15 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `weeks of maternity pay` 7 10 EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `weeks of maternity pay` 5 9 EQUALS 0
